    "title": "Young North Posey team looks to build their own legacy - NewsBreak",
    "text": "POSEYVILLE, Ind. (WEHT) – After the departure of some key seniors from last football season, North Posey is looking for some young players to make an impact this year. Head coach Waylon Schenk is looking to build off a seven and three record from a season ago. Despite the youth of the team, the Vikings are returning Junior Quarterback, Carter Schickel who started most of the 2024-2025 season. Coach Schenk says his team is eager to learn every day and could be one of the most coachable teams he’s had. The North Posey Vikings open up their season against Southridge, Aug 22. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to Eyewitness News (WEHT/WTVW).",
